ps","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T10:34:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-17T10:36:13Z","body":"I think it might be good to mention in the GDScript docs under \"referencing functions\", I did miss it in the main description of `Callable` though when looking for cases where this was clarified, would be good if there was a way to make that one stick out more","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3414892598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3415310379","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111754#issuecomment-3415310379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111754","id":3415310379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LkYAr","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T12:14:15Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T00:15:53Z","body":"> This is documented in the description of the `Callable` class and the `Callable.create()` method. We could add a note to the `Dictionary` class description, but that's all, I suppose?\n\nFor an error like:\n```\nError at (8, 42): Cannot find member \"erase\" in base \"Dictionary[int, int]\".\n```\nin case the base is non-Object type and such type has given method, maybe a suggestion to use `Callable.create` could be added to (after) the error?\n\n---\n\n<details><summary>Edited out part (as this is not a bug as mentioned below) </summary>\n<p>\n\n> This is an existing limitation, you need to use [`Callable.create`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_callable.html#class-callable-method-create)\n\nThat's one thing.\n\nBut there's another issue here, note that for the dictionary with string key it produces 2 errors, and the base object type reported in the error is the dictionary value type (changed to `Vector2` in my example to ensure it's the type of the value), not the dictionary itself:\n\n<img width=\"976\" height=\"343\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be2891dc-729c-4a0b-8336-23ac994864aa\" />|<img width=\"976\" height=\"343\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/872ae46a-e912-431e-88fd-800230bfd395\" />\n-|-\n\nAnd indeed it seems that the parser incorrectly treats `typed_dictionary.erase` as if it's of the value type (here `Vector2`), e.g. it doesn't error about `typed_dictionary.erase.angle()`:\n\n<img width=\"1039\" height=\"261\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cc41f901-6a0e-46d4-8ca4-eaed531e92ea\" />\n\n\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\nsignal test_signal\n\nvar typed_dictionary : Dictionary[String, Vector2]\n\nfunc test_function_number(key : String) -> void:\n\ttest_signal.connect(typed_dictionary.erase.bind(key))\n\t#test_signal.connect(typed_dictionary.erase.angle())\n```\n\n</p>\n</details> ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3415310379/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3892855869","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111754#issuecomment-3892855869","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111754","id":3892855869,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oCEQ9","user":{"login":"cdemirer","id":41021322,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDIxMzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41021322?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer","html_url":"https://github.com/cdemirer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdemirer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-12T19:04:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T19:04:14Z","body":"> it seems that the parser incorrectly treats typed_dictionary.erase as if it's of the value type (here Vector2), e.g. it doesn't error about typed_dictionary.erase.angle()\n\nIt looks correct to me that `typed_dictionary.erase` is assumed to be of type `Vector2`, since the dictionary is typed and the value type is defined to be `Vector2`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3892855869/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894090731","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111754#issuecomment-3894090731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111754","id":3894090731,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oGxvr","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T00:13:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T00:17:22Z","body":"> It looks correct to me that `typed_dictionary.erase` is assumed to be of type `Vector2`, since the dictionary is typed and the value type is defined to be `Vector2`.\n\nAbsolutely agree, after rereading that part of my comment it makes no sense to me now / I have the same conclusion as you. 🙃\nThanks for correcting!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3894090731/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]